.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "object-assign [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/object-assign.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/object-assign)"
.PP
.RS 4
ES2015 \fR\fRObject\&.assign()\fP\fP \fRponyfill\fP 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Use the built-in"
.PP
Node\&.js 4 and up, as well as every evergreen browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Opera, Safari), support \fRObject\&.assign()\fP :tada:\&. If you target only those environments, then by all means, use \fRObject\&.assign()\fP instead of this package\&.
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install \-\-save object\-assign
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const objectAssign = require('object\-assign');

objectAssign({foo: 0}, {bar: 1});
//=> {foo: 0, bar: 1}

// multiple sources
objectAssign({foo: 0}, {bar: 1}, {baz: 2});
//=> {foo: 0, bar: 1, baz: 2}

// overwrites equal keys
objectAssign({foo: 0}, {foo: 1}, {foo: 2});
//=> {foo: 2}

// ignores null and undefined sources
objectAssign({foo: 0}, null, {bar: 1}, undefined);
//=> {foo: 0, bar: 1}
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "objectAssign(target, [source, \&.\&.\&.])"
Assigns enumerable own properties of \fRsource\fP objects to the \fRtarget\fP object and returns the \fRtarget\fP object\&. Additional \fRsource\fP objects will overwrite previous ones\&.
